{"metadata":{"description":"Save-money plugin for DSH (DeepSeek Harness) — define your own "pause / resume" time windows; at pause time running long tasks are paused (not stopped) automatically, and they resume when the window ends.","id":"gh:1335082381","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-save-money","slug":"zhu168/dsh-save-money","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Save-money plugin for DSH (DeepSeek Harness) — define your own "pause / resume" time windows; at pau"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"se time running long tasks are paused (not stopped) automatically, and they resume when the window e"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"ime running long tasks are paused (not stopped) automatically, and they resume when the window ends."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-save-money"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Save-money plugin** for DSH (DeepSeek Harness) — define your own "pause / resume" time windows; at"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" pause time running long tasks are **paused** (not stopped) automatically, and they resume when the "},{"id":"p3s3","text":"window ends. Built for LLM API **peak/off-peak pricing** (e.g. DeepSeek peak hours 9:00–12:00, 14:00"},{"id":"p3s4","text":"–18:00 Beijing time, off-peak at half price; since **2026-08-23 weekends are off-peak all day** — th"},{"id":"p3s5","text":"e plugin's weekday switch skips Sat/Sun by default), and equally useful for time-of-use electricity "},{"id":"p3s6","text":"rates, bandwidth off-peak shifting, or any "I don't want the machine working during this period" sce"},{"id":"p3s7","text":" bandwidth off-peak shifting, or any "I don't want the machine working during this period" scenario."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> Status: ✅ Implemented, continuously maintained. 中文版"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Interface"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The colored status text in the top-right of the session header (Save · ⚪/🟢/🟡/🔴, color follows the st"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ate) is the single persistent entry — click it to open the settings popover. When a pause is upcomin"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"g or active, a reminder banner appears at the top of the page (with the **End this save mode** butto"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"r active, a reminder banner appears at the top of the page (with the **End this save mode** button)."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"With "Show balance" enabled, your official DeepSeek account balance appears next to the status text;"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" **clicking the balance** opens the last-8-hours spend bar chart:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Each bar is a 10-minute window: the X axis shows whole-hour ticks, the Y axis key-point amount ticks"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" (≤5, with gridlines), and hovering shows each window's exact time range and amount. Windows where t"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"he balance dropped without any local activity are marked in warning color (changes may come from ano"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"opped without any local activity are marked in warning color (changes may come from another device)."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- **Multiple time windows**: add / remove pause-resume windows freely; supports midnight-crossing wi"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ndows (23:00–08:00) and per-weekday filtering;
- **Automatic pause on schedule**: when the pause tim"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"e arrives, running tasks are safely "frozen" (their progress is preserved exactly — nothing is inter"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"rupted or lost) and resume automatically when the window ends; **if nothing is running, nothing is p"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"aused**;
- **No requests during the window (the saving core)**: inside a pause window the AI sends n"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"o new requests to the model service, so **no cost is incurred**; after the window ends (or on disabl"},{"id":"p10s7","text":"e / end-this-window) everything resumes, with conversation context and in-flight tasks unaffected. *"},{"id":"p10s8","text":"*The AI not replying inside a window (including new conversations) is expected** — to resume right a"},{"id":"p10s9","text":"way, click the **End this save mode** button (takes effect directly, no AI involved);
- **Per-model-"},{"id":"p10s10","text":"tier save mode**: decide per model tier which ones pause during windows. The settings panel shows tw"},{"id":"p10s11","text":"o compact rows — **Official API** (the DeepSeek official API) and **Other API** (EVERY non-official "},{"id":"p10s12","text":"provider: opencode go/zen, relays, SiliconFlow, …) — each with **flash / pro / vision** toggles (vis"},{"id":"p10s13","text":"ion = `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp`), six toggles total. Checked = paused (saving money); unchecked"},{"id":"p10s14","text":" = **exempt** (requests flow even during a window). Defaults: the three official tiers checked, all "},{"id":"p10s15","text":""other" tiers exempt; your changes are persisted and never reset. Any model whose name carries no fl"},{"id":"p10s16","text":"ash/pro/vision marker (legacy `chat`/`reasoner`, unknown models, anything else) is always exempt — i"},{"id":"p10s17","text":"t can never block your requests;
- **Global weekday switch**: one row above the window list — 一 ☑️ 二"},{"id":"p10s18","text":" ☑️ 三 ☑️ 四 ☑️ 五 ☑️ 六 ⬜ 日 ⬜. Saving applies only on the checked days (default **Mon–Fri** — under the"},{"id":"p10s19","text":" 2026-08-23 peak/off-peak rule weekends are off-peak all day, so nothing pauses on Sat/Sun). Compose"},{"id":"p10s20","text":"d with each window's own per-weekday filter: both must match for a window to apply;
[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- When a pause window starts, running tasks are frozen (progress preserved) and the AI stops replyin"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"g — that is normal: the machine is saving you money. Everything resumes automatically when the windo"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"w ends;
- See the yellow "pause in X min" banner but don't want to pause right now? Click **End this"},{"id":"p13s4","text":" save mode** to cancel this window only;
- Paused and want to continue immediately? Click **End this"},{"id":"p13s5","text":" save mode** (red button) — it resumes right away, skips only the current window, and never turns of"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"f **Enable**: the next window (today or later) still saves money as usual. If you ever want every wi"},{"id":"p13s7","text":"ndow to take effect again, uncheck and re-check **Enable**."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Install from npm (recommended)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The plugin is published to npm — one command installs it into your Web profile:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"#### First-time install"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Path 3: development workflow (what this repository actually uses: link install + HMR hot reload)"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Changes take effect immediately — **no DSH restart** and no tgz needed. This is the form used while "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"developing the plugin: `dsh plugin add link:` links the `plugin/` directory straight into the profil"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"e, and a `cordis-plugin-hmr` hot-reload plugin watches the build output. Save the source → `npm run "},{"id":"p21s4","text":"prepare` → the running DSH hot-swaps the new plugin; hard-refresh the browser to see the client UI."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"**One-time setup (on the development machine):**"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"1. Build and link-install:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"2. Configure hot reload: edit `~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml` (create it if missing) and repl"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ace `root` with your repository's `plugin` directory absolute path:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"3. Start DSH (`pnpm dsh web` / `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`) and open the browser (default http://127."},{"id":"p27s2","text":" (`pnpm dsh web` / `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`) and open the browser (default http://127.0.0.1:3080)."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"**Daily dev loop:**"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"DSH hot-replaces the plugin within ~0.1s (look for `[hmr]` logs in the terminal) — **no restart**; *"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"*hard-refresh the browser (Ctrl+Shift+R)** to see client-side changes."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"> Note: `link:` and the Path 2 bundle install are mutually exclusive — if you installed the bundle b"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"efore, run `pnpm dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-save-money` first, then `add link:`."}],"truncated":true}
